            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-33",
                    "linecount": 70,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 580.0, 1029.0 ],
                    "text": "================================================================================\nchorus_psychoacoustic_hyperbolic_itd — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nOVERVIEW\nA standalone stereo Psychoacoustic ITD Chorus implementing William L. Martens and Atsushi Marui's \"Categories of Perception for Vibrato, Flange, and Stereo Chorus: Mapping out the Musically Useful Ranges of Modulation Rate and Depth for Delay-based Effects\" (DAFx-06 Paper p_149, Sections 1, 2.1 & 3, Eq. 1–3, Fig. 1–2). Built around two perceptual findings from the paper:\n1. Constant Pitch-Excursion Hyperbola (Section 3, Fig. 2): Through logistic regression on listening tests, Martens and Marui proved that the lower and upper boundaries of the \"musically useful\" chorus region follow a hyperbola where modulation depth (in microseconds) scales linearly with modulation period `1 / Rate_Hz`:\n   `Depth_lower(us) = 814 / Rate_Hz - 66` and `Depth_upper(us) = 4800 / Rate_Hz - 350`.\n   By automatically sliding modulation depth along this hyperbola as you turn `mod_rate_hz`, the peak Doppler pitch deviation `alpha(t) = 1 +/- 2*pi*DEPTH*RATE` (Eq. 2) stays locked in the musical sweet spot at any speed from 0.4 Hz to 9.0 Hz!\n2. ITD Lead/Lag Spatial Orbit (Section 2.1): By delaying the unmodulated dry signal by ~0.55 ms, the modulated chorus signal fluctuates symmetrically between LEADING (arriving earlier than) and LAGGING (arriving later than) the dry reference within the +/- 0.65 ms human Interaural Time Delay (ITD) window, causing the tuba to orbit smoothly around the listener's head.\n\nINLETS & OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: Stereo Audio Input (Tuba; mono in1 auto-normalizes to stereo)\n- in3: Optional Envelope Modulator [0..1] (pushes `perceptual_zone` toward the upper boundary on loud notes)\n- in4: Optional 1-Bar Audio-Rate Phasor [0..1] (syncs primary LFO when patched)\n- out1 / out2: Stereo ITD Lead/Lag Hyperbolic Chorus Output\n\nPARAMETERS (6)\n\n1. mod_rate_hz\n   - Range: 0.40 to 9.00 Hz (Delay Modulation Rate, Default: 3.20 Hz, spanning the DAFx-06 2–9 Hz factorial test range)\n   - Taper: Direct frequency in Hz.\n   - Function: Controls the modulation speed while automatically adjusting modulation depth along the Fig. 2 regression curve when `rate_depth_coupling > 0`.\n\n2. perceptual_zone\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (Position Between \"Sub-Useful\" Lower Boundary 0.0, Optimal Musical Center 0.5, and \"Supra-Useful\" Upper Boundary 1.0; Default: 0.55)\n   - Taper: Linear interpolation between the DAFx-06 Fig. 2 lower and upper logit boundary equations.\n   - Function: Lets you dial in the exact psychoacoustic intensity (\"subtle\", \"musical sweet spot\", or \"extreme\") regardless of LFO speed.\n\n3. rate_depth_coupling\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0.0 = Uncoupled Manual Depth, 1.0 = Full DAFx-06 Fig. 2 Inverse-Rate Hyperbolic Coupling; Default: 0.85)\n   - Taper: Linear coupling blend.\n   - Function: Keeps pitch excursion constant when sweeping `mod_rate_hz` with a macro knob or expression pedal.\n\n4. itd_center_ms\n   - Range: 0.20 to 2.50 ms (Unmodulated Reference Delay for ITD Lead/Lag Orbit, Default: 0.55 ms matching DAFx-06 Section 2.1's 0.5 ms ITD center)\n   - Taper: Direct delay time in milliseconds.\n   - Function: Sets the baseline reference delay about which the modulated chorus voices lead (arrive early) and lag (arrive late).\n\n5. voice_quadrature\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (Stereo Quadrature Phase & Secondary Voice Blend, Default: 0.65)\n   - Taper: Linear stereo phase & dual-voice depth.\n   - Function: Controls the binaural circularity of the ITD head-orbit illusion.\n\n6. dry_wet_mix\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (Reference Dry vs. Leading/Lagging Modulated Voices; Default: 0.50 = Maximum ITD Stereo Chorus)\n   - Taper: Constant-power cosine/sine crossfade.\n   - Function: At 0.50, equalizes the time-delayed dry reference and the leading/lagging modulated voices for maximum binaural precedence-effect width.\n",
                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                }
            }
